      <h2>What each term does</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>TVL</b> is the size the market has already put behind the protocol. It is the base, not the answer.</li>
        <li><b>Momentum</b> is TVL's seven-day change, clamped to −60%…+120% and weighted at half. It moves the value in the direction the deposits are already going.</li>
        <li><b>Maturity</b> rises with age from 0.55 to 1.00 over three years, because a protocol that has survived more snapshots has proved more of its claims.</li>
        <li><b>Breadth</b> adds 3% per chain up to four, for protocols that raised capital across more than one chain.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the board does not claim</h2>
      <div class="callout warn">A protocol's implied value is this entry's own estimate of what its token would be worth if the record stayed as it is. It is not a prediction that a token is issued, not a forecast of when, and not advice to farm or to buy. The snapshot records no token for any protocol on the board; a protocol may hold one the snapshot does not carry.</div>
      <p style="margin-top:12px">The model is deterministic: the same snapshot always yields the same board, the same ranks and the same bytes, and the judge sees the same three renders on every run.</p>
